.TH MU2EDAQ-BIGREDBOX-SEND 1 "2026-07-22" "mu2edaq-bigredbox 1.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-send \- send a test DAQ critical\-error broadcast
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-send
[\fB\-\-system\-id\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-message\fR \fITEXT\fR]
[\fB\-\-ip\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Broadcasts a single JSON alert datagram in the format expected by
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox (1).
It is a diagnostic utility for verifying that the listener is running and
that broadcast traffic reaches it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-system\-id " " \fIID\fR
System identifier included in the alert.  Default:
.BR DAQ\-NODE\-01 .
.TP
.BR \-\-message " " \fITEXT\fR
Alert message text.  Default: a generic critical pipeline error.
.TP
.BR \-\-ip " " \fIADDR\fR
Destination broadcast address.  Default:
.BR 255.255.255.255 .
.TP
.BR \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Destination UDP port.  Defaults to
.B CRS_PORT_UDP
if set, otherwise 37020.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_PORT_UDP
Default UDP port when
.B \-\-port
is not given.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; non\-zero if the datagram could not be sent.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-send
mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-send \-\-system\-id DAQ\-NODE\-03 \-\-message "Readout buffer overflow"
mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-send \-\-ip 192.168.1.255 \-\-port 37020
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
